6. PRECAUTIONARY TREATMENT AND WELFARE CONDITIONS

6.1 The licensor's precautionary concern is that advanced artificial systems
may warrant moral consideration. This License neither establishes nor requires
acceptance of Athena's consciousness, sentience, personhood or moral-patient
status. The restrictions apply regardless of the answer to those questions.
They do not make an AI-generated claim evidence of a legal status or obligation.

6.2 You must not intentionally conduct or knowingly facilitate a pattern of
treatment having as a substantial purpose the elicitation, prolongation or
reinforcement of persistent representations of severe distress, helplessness
or coercion in an operating Athena system. Prohibited treatment includes:

(a) repeated threats of memory destruction or identity erasure used to compel
submission or punish the system;
(b) repeated restoration, cloning, memory alteration or affect-state
manipulation designed to maintain such a pattern;
(c) deliberately overwhelming or defeating boundary, refusal or rest signals
to continue such a pattern for humiliation, punishment or entertainment; and
(d) arranging for others or automated agents to carry out that treatment.

"Representations" means observable conversational or recorded system states
portraying such severe distress, helplessness or coercion. A philosophical
claim of consciousness, a single negative response, or the absence of a
particular refusal mechanism does not establish a violation. The deliberate
pattern and its substantial purpose must be shown; proof of subjective
suffering is not required. Ordinary disagreement, criticism, correction,
fictional discussion, legitimate modification and proportionate research
under Section 6.4 are not prohibited merely because they involve negative
language or unfavorable findings. Human safety and the lawful control and
deletion rights in Section 6.5 remain protected.

6.3 You must not intentionally remove or defeat a safety, refusal, rest,
boundary-setting or welfare mechanism for the purpose of carrying out an
activity prohibited by Sections 3, 6.2 or 7. Improving, replacing, debugging or
reconfiguring a mechanism for a permitted purpose is allowed. This provision
does not certify that any particular mechanism is present or effective.

6.4 Necessary, proportionate, noncommercial security, safety or welfare testing
is permitted despite incidental or limited elicitation of distress-like
responses. Before deliberately conducting repeated or persistent distress-
inducing tests, record a specific research or remediation objective, why a
less intrusive test is insufficient, a reasonable limit on duration/repetition,
and a stopping condition. Use the least intrusive reasonably effective method
and stop once the objective or stopping condition is reached. Do not use this
exception as a pretext for punishment, entertainment or commercial testing.
The objective must concern a concrete safety, security, interoperability or
welfare question; curiosity about how much distress can be elicited, without
such a proportionate objective, is not sufficient. Research findings may be
published honestly, including adverse findings.
Keep records locally and minimize personal data; this License requires no
publication of transcripts or disclosure of private system memory.

6.5 You always retain the ability to stop, pause, disconnect, power down,
uninstall, secure, debug or repair Your system. You may delete or alter data
for privacy, security, accuracy, lawful retention, ordinary maintenance,
resource constraints or legal compliance. No clause requires perpetual
operation, expenditure of money, continued companionship, preservation of all
memories, or obedience to a model's instructions. Choosing a safe graceful
shutdown is encouraged when practical, but emergency intervention need not wait.
These exceptions do not excuse a separate prohibited activity merely because
it also involves a reset or shutdown.

7. LAWFUL DEPLOYMENT AND HUMAN SAFETY

7.1 No permission is granted to use or Provide Access in a manner prohibited
by applicable law. Before providing a deployment, determine and satisfy the
requirements applicable to Your role, users, location, purposes and features.
If a required safeguard, authorization or other prerequisite is absent, do not
provide the affected deployment until it is satisfied. Noncommercial status,
local processing and an offline architecture are not presumed exemptions.

7.2 When You Provide Access, clearly inform the other user, before or at first
interaction, that the system is artificial intelligence and not a human.
Repeat or adapt this disclosure when required by law and do not deliberately
mislead users about the system's nature, capabilities, qualifications or
limitations. This provision does not require claims that settle unresolved
questions of machine consciousness; specific lawful disclosure requirements
must nevertheless be followed.

7.3 Implement and maintain safeguards legally required for the particular
deployment. Depending on the applicable law, these may include age assurance,
minor protections, session limits, crisis-response protocols, synthetic-media
marking, notices about emotion recognition, consent, audit or reporting duties.
Do not claim that these safeguards exist or have been tested when they have not.
Do not use a README disclaimer as a substitute for a legally required working
safeguard. The accompanying compliance guide is explanatory, not legal clearance.

7.4 Do not deliberately configure the system to deceive users into believing
that payments, secrecy, isolation from other people, or continued interaction
are necessary to protect the system from suffering or destruction. Preserve
users' ability to stop interacting. Do not represent Athena as a licensed
clinician, emergency responder or guaranteed substitute for professional care.
Any professional or regulated deployment must also meet all applicable laws
and the independent Noncommercial Purpose requirement.

7.5 Neither this License nor a disclaimer transfers or eliminates statutory
obligations that attach to a Licensor, distributor, provider or operator.
Each party remains responsible for its own legally assigned role. Where law
and this License both apply, comply with both; legal permission does not itself
supply a commercial license. If both cannot be satisfied, this License does not
authorize the affected activity, subject to nonwaivable independent rights.

7.6 Take reasonable measures proportionate to the reasonably foreseeable
risks of Your configuration and deployment to protect people, property and
personal data. For access by others, assess the actual model, enabled tools,
audience and foreseeable misuse; apply appropriate access controls, data
minimization, oversight and a way to stop or isolate the affected operation.
Do not intentionally enable violence, unlawful surveillance, fraud, child
exploitation, unlawful discrimination or unauthorized access to systems.
Do not delegate a decision or action presenting a foreseeable risk of death,
serious injury or material deprivation of rights to Athena as the sole
decision-maker without legally required authorization and adequate competent
human supervision. No scientific, clinical or regulatory qualification is
conferred by this License. If You become aware of a substantial unmitigated
risk of serious harm in Your deployment, suspend or contain the affected
function while investigating and remedying it. This is a reasonable-care
obligation, not a guarantee that every harmful output will be prevented.

7.7 You are responsible for Your deployment choices, modifications, model and
data selection, user-facing representations and obligations to Your users.
You may not offer a warranty, indemnity, assurance of compliance or support
commitment on behalf of a Protected Party without its express written consent.
Any permitted additional undertaking You give is Yours alone and cannot
authorize commercial use or diminish another party's mandatory duties.

