11. DURATION, TERMINATION AND CURE

11.1 Compliant grants continue for their stated duration and are not withdrawn
merely because a Licensor stops maintaining the project or publishes another
license version. Permissions under this License automatically terminate upon
Your material breach, subject to Section 11.2. You must stop prohibited activity
when You become aware of it; no cure period authorizes continuing it.

11.2 For a first, unintentional breach, permissions automatically reinstate
prospectively when You fully remedy the breach within 30 days after first
learning of it, provided it is reasonably capable of remedy. Intentional
commercial exploitation, intentional conduct prohibited by Section 6.2 or 7,
and repeated material violations do not qualify for automatic reinstatement.
Any other reinstatement requires express written action by the relevant
Licensor. Reinstatement does not erase liability already incurred or bind
third-party rights holders.

11.3 Termination affects only permissions under this License. It does not
terminate independent licenses or the grants to compliant downstream recipients.
You may retain an inactive archival copy for legal evidence, security response
or orderly transition, but may not resume otherwise unlicensed operation.
Safe shutdown, legally required actions and nonwaivable rights remain available.
Sections 5 and 9 continue to apply to retained or redistributed material as
appropriate. Sections 12 through 16 and all accrued obligations, including
Section 14 for conduct during the relevant period, survive termination.
Termination does not authorize destruction of evidence required by law.

